    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "547:3068",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Amusement Park",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Amusement Park"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thrills and Fun\n\nFor my birthday, my parents took me and two friends to an amusement park. We arrived when the gates opened at ten o'clock so we could make the most of the day.\n\nThe first ride we tried was the roller coaster. We waited in a queue for about twenty minutes before it was our turn. The ride started slowly as the car climbed to the top of the first hill. Then it dropped steeply and raced through loops, twists, and sharp turns. My friends screamed the whole time, but I just laughed.\n\nAfter that, we went on the bumper cars. Each person drives a small electric car and tries to bump into the other cars. It was chaotic but hilarious. We also tried the spinning teacups ride, which made us quite dizzy.\n\nAt lunchtime, we stopped at a food stall and bought burgers, chips, and lemonade. The prices were expensive, but we were too hungry to care. We sat on a bench near the Ferris wheel and watched it turn slowly against the blue sky.\n\nIn the afternoon, we visited the haunted house attraction. It was dark inside, with spooky sounds, flashing lights, and actors dressed as ghosts who jumped out to scare us. One of my friends grabbed my arm so tightly that he left a mark!\n\nBefore leaving, we played some carnival games. I tried to knock down tin cans with a ball and won a small stuffed bear. My friend tried the hook-a-duck game and won a goldfish in a bag.\n\nWe left the park at six o'clock, exhausted but happy. It was the best birthday I have ever had.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Thrills and Fun For my birthday, my parents took me and two friends to an amusement park. We arrived when the gates opened at ten o'clock so we could make the most of the day. The first ride we tried was the roller coaster. We waited in a queue for about twenty minutes before it was our turn. The ride started slowly as the car climbed to the top of the first hill. Then it dropped steeply and raced through loops, twists, and sharp turns. My friends screamed the whole time, but I just laughed. After that, we went on the bumper cars. Each person drives a small electric car and tries to bump into the other cars. It was chaotic but hilarious. We also tried the spinning teacups ride, which made us quite dizzy. At lunchtime, we stopped at a food stall and bought burgers, chips, and lemonade. The prices were expensive, but we were too hungry to care. We sat on a bench near the Ferris wheel and watched it turn slowly against the blue sky. In the afternoon, we visited the haunted house attraction. It was dark inside, with spooky sounds, flashing lights, and actors dressed as ghosts who jumped out to scare us. One of my friends grabbed my arm so tightly that he left a mark! Before leaving, we played some carnival games. I tried to knock down tin cans with a ball and won a small stuffed bear. My friend tried the hook-a-duck game and won a goldfish in a bag. We left the park at six o'clock, exhausted but happy. It was the best birthday I have ever had."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. Why did they arrive when the park opened?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. Why did they arrive when the park opened?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What happens on a roller coaster ride?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What happens on a roller coaster ride?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What made the narrator dizzy?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What made the narrator dizzy?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What happened in the haunted house?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What happened in the haunted house?"
        },
        {
